228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E (The purpose of this project is to create a light but structurally strong landing system for a rover that will explore the lava caves on the Moon. The landing system will include an 8U CubeSat rover \(approximately 10 kg in weight\), within the total system mass of 15 kg, deployed using an airbag-based landing mechanism inspired by missions like Mars Pathfinder and Mars Exploration Rover.  The primary challenge is to design the rigid inner structure that will endure the forces of landing while remaining very light. This includes studying different geometric configurations of the structure, such as the tetrahedron and cube shapes, choosing the right materials, and studying the forces acting on the structure.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
