232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (This project results in the formulation of analytical sizing equations to determine structural dimensions based on impact conditions, material properties, and geometry. It includes evaluation of different structural configurations and materials to optimise mass and strength. A complete conceptual design of the lander can be established, including integration with the descent module, rover payload, and airbag system, along with identification of subsystem interactions. It is also expected to generate CAD models representing both the stowed and deployed configurations of the lander. A key outcome is the comparison of structural designs, showing that tetrahedral structures are more efficient than cubic ones due to axial load transfer, while cubic designs are governed by bending and buckling.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
