236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (The discovery of lunar lava caves is considered to be very promising since they can serve as a shelter against the harmful effects of solar radiation, micrometeorites, and extreme temperature changes. It makes them attractive sites of future habitation and exploration activities on the Moon. But to explore these places, one should have efficient robots with the ability to land safely on the surface. Traditional landing systems are often complex and mass-intensive, making them unsuitable for small-scale missions. Airbag landing systems offer a practical alternative, being lightweight and having been successfully utilized in earlier planetary missions. This research is aimed at addressing the problems associated with designing airbag systems that are sturdy enough to withstand landing impacts during small-scale lunar missions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
