/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (For structural analysis, two structures were considered: pyramidal \(tetrahedral\) structure and cube-shaped structure. The pyramidal structure was modeled as an axial loading problem, whereby loads act on the edges and the structural elements, hence giving rise to a membrane stress condition. Conversely, the cube-shaped structure was modeled as a series of plane sections undergoing bending, hence increasing the likelihood of yielding and buckling.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
