/E (A key outcome of the study is that buckling is the dominating factor affecting the structure thickness and should be considered in addition to stress. Numerical evaluation for the given mission parameters shows that impact forces are on the order of hundreds of Newtons, with resulting pressures in the kilopascal range. The tetrahedral structure consistently requires lower thickness compared to the cubic configuration, making it more mass-efficient.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
